class:: VelvetFDNModel
summary:: Prepared sparse input/output or paraunitary velvet FDN topology
categories:: UGens>Reverbs, Libraries>CamaraObscura
related:: Guides/CamaraObscura, Classes/VelvetFDN

description::

VelvetFDNModel prepares fixed sparse FIR taps around an FDN or a lossless
filtered feedback structure. In paraunitary mode the feedback scattering is
code::H D(z) H::, where code::H:: is a normalized Hadamard transform and
code::D(z):: contains pure delays. Therefore its frequency response is
unitary before decay filters. The structure is informed by the filtered
feedback-matrix work of Schlecht and Habets and by the velvet-noise FDN work
of Fagerström, Alary, Schlecht, and Välimäki.

The closest vanilla architecture is an allpass-diffused delay network. This
model uses deterministic sparse taps and a tested paraunitary construction
instead of cascaded scalar allpasses.

classmethods::

method:: default
Prepare sparse input and output velvet filters around a conventional FDN.

argument:: delayCount
Fixed line count from 2 through 32.

argument:: t60
Low-band T60 in seconds; the high-band target is 65 percent of this value.

argument:: sampleRate
Exact server sample rate.

argument:: seed
Deterministic delay and tap seed.

method:: filteredMatrix
Prepare an explicit-delay model.

argument:: delays
Delay seconds when below 2, otherwise sample counts.

argument:: velvetFilters
Its flattened size selects one through 16 sparse taps in this first format.
Tap positions and signs remain deterministic rather than being copied from
this argument.

argument:: attenuationFilters
Two values interpreted as low/high T60.

argument:: feedbackStructure
Use code::\paraunitary:: for code::H D(z) H:: feedback; any other symbol
selects input/output filtering.

argument:: sampleRate
Exact renderer sample rate.

argument:: seed
Deterministic delay and sparse-tap seed.

method:: read
Read a version-1 VelvetFDN model.

instancemethods::

method:: validate
Validate metadata, line data, sparse taps, and optional scattering delays.

method:: summary
Return concise diagnostics.

method:: load
Upload the model to a mono Buffer.

method:: write
Serialize the model.

method:: free
Free the last uploaded Buffer.

examples::

code::
(
var model = VelvetFDNModel.default(
    8, 3.5, sampleRate: 48000, seed: 9
);
[model.modeName, model.summary].postln;
)
::

code::
(
var model = VelvetFDNModel.filteredMatrix(
    [0.037, 0.043, 0.051, 0.059],
    0 ! 12,
    [2.8, 1.4],
    \paraunitary,
    sampleRate: 48000,
    seed: 4
);
model.validate;
[model.modeName, model.summary].postln;
)
::

